---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms"
  description="Don't use Gridwatch to guess future electricity prices, or to decide if the power system is safe. We can get things wrong."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <h2>Forecasting</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use this data for forecasting. Forecasting means guessing what
      electricity prices will do next, or how much power the country will use or
      make. Gridwatch looks at what already happened.
    </p>
    <h2>Safety-critical decisions</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use this data for safety-critical decisions. That's work where a
      wrong number could hurt people or the power system, like deciding whether
      the power system is safe, when to run a power station, or how to operate
      it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Gridwatch is independent. We aren't the Electricity Authority, the
      government body that sets the rules for the electricity market, and we
      aren't the grid operator, the people who keep the lights on.
    </p>
    <p>
      The numbers come from EMI (the Authority's public electricity data). We
      can still get things wrong. If you need an official figure, get it from
      EMI.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure-prose);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }
</style>
